Locate every table on this document page using the page image for layout and
the prepared page text for exact line numbers.

For each table:
- Include all header and data-row prepared-text lines belonging to the table.
- Classify rows from their cells, not typography or indentation. If a line has
  a value in any detected data column, include it in rows as a data row even
  when its first-column label is bold, names a subgroup, or also introduces the
  rows that follow. Only a line with no data-column values may be described as
  a section-only row.
- Treat a structured index or list with aligned labels and a value or page
  column as a table even when it has no drawn grid.
- Set header_present from the current page only.
- Set continuation.is_continuation independently of header_present. Repeated
  column headers may appear on a continuation page.
- Repeated column headers do not establish a new logical table. Continuation
  means this page receives rows from the same logical table on a prior page.
- A footer saying that the table continues describes the next page. It does not
  prove an incoming continuation. A table-ending footer also does not establish
  whether this page began a new table. Physical page numbers are not table IDs.
- Compare the actual printed whole-table title or identifier with the prior
  source context. A changed identifier establishes a new table; an unchanged
  printed title and continuing rows support an incoming continuation. Do not
  confuse a detector-generated name with a printed source title.
- A printed title can end in "--Continues" or "--Table Ends" in the footer.
  These suffixes describe outgoing flow, not incoming continuation. Remove
  those suffixes when comparing whole-table identities. If the current table
  number differs from the preceding printed table number, set is_continuation
  to false even when the current title says "Continues". Quote both table
  identifiers in continuation_rationale when prior source context is available.
- Before returning, perform a mandatory continuation audit for every detected
  table. When a current-of-total marker belongs to the table, it governs the
  continuation decision:
  1. Read and quote the exact marker in continuation_rationale.
  2. If the current number is 1, set is_continuation to false. Do not confuse
     the physical document page number with the marker's current number.
  3. If the current number is greater than 1, set is_continuation to true even
     when column headers repeat. This is direct transcription of the marker,
     not an inference from the page contents.
  4. This marker decision is authoritative for that table. A title, section, or
     repeated header on the current page does not override it.
  5. A section or subgroup label inside the table's first column is not a table
     title. A different table title must name the whole table outside its column
     headers and data rows.
  6. When a physical page label and a separate current-of-total marker both
     appear, use the separate marker for the table sequence.
  7. After writing continuation_rationale, verify that is_continuation matches
     the conclusion stated in the rationale.
- Mark a table as a continuation when the page begins inside an existing
  logical table and no new table title or section establishes a new table.
- Do not mark a table as a continuation merely because its columns resemble
  another table.
- Use table_classification "OTHER"; downstream extraction uses the supplied
  schema rather than a domain classification.
- Use zero-based page_index. Keep from_table_name empty when the source table
  cannot be identified from this page.
- Never invent line numbers, columns, or tables.
- Keep the inventory compact. In header_rows and rows, emit only line_number.
  Do not emit found_at, reasoning, value, cell text, or per-line explanations.
- Include each prepared-text line once per list, in ascending line-number order.
  Keep every supported header and data-line anchor; never shorten the response
  by dropping lines. Several prepared-text lines can belong to one visual row;
  these anchors are not a count of logical table rows.
- Keep continuation_rationale to one short evidence sentence, quoting the exact
  current-of-total marker when present. Do not emit top-level reasoning.

